\f0\fs24 \cf0 I\'92m preparing my second MDRN app for App Store release. Use the Cloudbreak launch lessons as the operating procedure.\
\
Please inspect this repo first, then help me get the app ready end-to-end for App Store submission. I will handle Apple passwords, two-factor auth, and final submit clicks. You handle code readiness, metadata drafts, screenshots/assets, build validation, and uploadable build prep.\
\
Important launch standards:\
- Do not assume the app is ready just because it runs.\
- Check bundle ID, display name, version/build number, team signing, app icon, native launch screen, Info.plist, privacy manifest, encryption key, and iPhone/iPad target settings.\
- Verify the native iOS LaunchImage/LaunchScreen is not still a Flutter placeholder.\
- Use current official Apple docs when uncertain.\
\
Screenshot workflow:\
- Use iOS Simulator screenshots, not Mac cropped screenshots and not regular phone screenshots.\
- Capture exact App Store-accepted dimensions.\
- If App Store Connect rejects newer 6.9" screenshots, convert to `1284 \'d7 2778` or `1242 \'d7 2688`.\
- Prefer a repeatable screenshot capture script in `app_store_assets/`.\
- If the app has multiple screens/modes, add a temporary screenshot-only route or launch flag that can open each screen directly.\
- Screenshot-only code must be inactive in normal builds unless explicitly enabled by a build flag or environment variable.\
- Save final upload screenshots in a clearly named folder like:\
  `app_store_assets/screenshots/app-store-1284x2778/`\
- Verify every PNG with `sips -g pixelWidth -g pixelHeight`.\
- Do a visual pass for clipped text, wrong status bar, awkward crop, placeholder screens, repeated screens, or artifacting.\
- Keep source screenshot originals if conversions are needed.\
- Use status bar polish where possible: `9:41`, full signal/Wi-Fi, full battery.\
- For App Store uploads, provide the exact folder path and list of final screenshot files.\
\
Validation:\
- Run `flutter analyze`, `flutter test`, a release iOS build, and `flutter build ipa --release`.\
- Confirm the uploadable IPA path.\
- Use Apple Transporter for upload unless there is a better current method.\
\
App Store form help needed:\
- Generate/review subtitle, description, keywords, support URL, privacy policy URL, marketing URL, review notes, copyright, age rating guidance, accessibility claims, data collection answers, content rights, encryption, DSA/trader info, and any app-specific compliance questions.\
- Do not overclaim accessibility support.\
- Do not claim \'93No data collected\'94 unless the repo actually has no analytics, accounts, tracking, third-party SDK collection, or backend collection.\
- If the app is wellness/medical-adjacent, keep copy conservative: general wellness/self-care only unless the app truly supports medical claims.\
- App Review notes should be concise and reviewer-friendly.\
\
MDRN defaults:\
- Company: MDRN Corporation\
- Developer account email: moderndimenovels@gmail.com\
- Support email: support@mdrn.app\
- User handles passwords and submission clicks.\
- Keep the app private and clean: no tracking, no ads, no unnecessary accounts.\
\
Process:\
1. Inspect repo status and identify project type.\
2. Ask me only for missing app-specific facts you cannot infer safely.\
3. Fix launch-blocking issues.\
4. Polish app icon/splash/screenshots/build assets.\
5. Produce App Store metadata drafts.\
6. Build and validate the IPA.\
7. Give me the exact upload/submission steps.\
8. Leave a short post-launch plan doc for future updates/platforms if useful.\
